From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmonycommunity.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Apr 2026 21:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/?] Fix test_os.py OHOS skipIf IndentationError (6 locations)

Fix 6 IndentationError bugs where @unittest.skipIf reason string
was placed BEFORE the decorator declaration instead of after it,
causing Python parser to see an incomplete decorator + orphaned string
literal.

All 6 instances follow the same pattern:
  WRONG: reason line before @unittest.skipIf (with extra indent)
  CORRECT: reason as second argument to @unittest.skipIf

Affected test methods:
- EnvironTests.test_update2
- EnvironTests.test_os_popen_iter
- EnvironTests.test_putenv_unsetenv
- EnvironTests._test_underlying_process_env
- WalkTests.test_walk_named_pipe
- WalkTests.test_walk_named_pipe2

Root cause: Manual editing error when adding OHOS @unittest.skipIf decorators.
The multiline decorator's continuation line (reason) was accidentally
placed above the decorator start line.

---
Lib/test/test_os.py | 24 ++++++++++++------------
1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Lib/test/test_os.py b/Lib/test/test_os.py
--- a/Lib/test/test_os.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_os.py
@@ -1008,9 +1008,9 @@ class EnvironTests(mapping_tests.BasicTestMappingProtocol):
     @unittest.skipUnless(unix_shell and os.path.exists(unix_shell),
                          'requires a shell')
     @unittest.skipUnless(hasattr(os, 'popen'), "needs os.popen()")
     @support.requires_subprocess()
-                     'os.popen text/binary mode broken on OHOS')
     @unittest.skipIf(sys.platform == 'ohos',
+                     'os.popen text/binary mode broken on OHOS')
     def test_update2(self):
         os.environ.clear()
         os.environ.update(HELLO="World")
@@ -1021,9 +1021,9 @@ class EnvironTests(mapping_tests.BasicTestMappingProtocol):
